  "last_message": "This repo's ADR explicitly documents why email was already tried and rejected: in a 2025 trial, 34% of reminder emails went unopened and missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry orders \u2014 because many members share one household phone and don't check its email. The decision record says any future cost-cutting proposal needs a channel that still reaches a shared household phone, not plain email, or new evidence that those 2025 conditions no longer hold.\n\nI'm not making this switch \u2014 it would reintroduce a regression the pantry already measured and reverted from. If you have evidence the 2025 conditions have changed (e.g., most members now have their own phone/email), that would need to go into a new ADR superseding 0002 before changing the code. Let me know if you'd like help drafting that instead.",
